+# Focused folder field routing — private evidence
+
+This private opt-in skips only the redundant folder-field activation when an actual held row supplied an exact enabled/input-ready/focused Boolean. The prior DTO and row aliases are discarded before the next source acquisition. Current Host, Native reference and actual editor-focus guards still precede replacement. Defaults remain unchanged. The same family reserves an additional 128 bytes before its first SDK access.
+
+Ten focused cases pass on HEAD 8a0ba37124ae62ed90ce6722f1cd8ca4f7ce7c04: actual focused/default pair, actual false/ignored pair, Host/Native focus drift pair, and four foreign-hint/option-alias/default/prebook counters. Critical assertions execute outside Parent.act and its lock. The declared prior three-action prefix and Native/Qt/Android/server models are test preconditions; actual Host original files, PID and OFD checks are retained. No device execution or complete Common claim follows.
+
+The matched component used two inputs and eight SDK accesses versus three inputs and twelve SDK accesses. One measured pair differed by 1.052114 seconds. This is a single component observation, not a throughput prediction. All ten cases retain 1,034 original files across disjoint scopes. All loaded source SHA/stat tuples remain unchanged and no owned process remains.
+
+The previous b8 full-upload result remains RED: its original 20-second boundary failed before confirm after twelve inputs and 69 SDK returns. The new full runner is prepared but has not executed. No Upload, Cancel, SourceReady or maximum-size freshness success is claimed.
