+# Fresh strict JSON pair comparison — proposal only
+
+No repository/native/source mutation or owning run. This is one pure function beside the existing pure canonical_size, not a new class/module/runner or an owner. It grants no Lifecycle/Assets authority. It validates BOTH current graphs through the exact existing canonical_size on every call, then compares exact built-in key/type/scalar values without full canonical buffers or cached verdicts. Aliases are allowed; cycles/nonfinite/foreign values fail in the existing validator; ensure_ascii=True means valid escaped lone surrogates remain representable. Finite float repr preserves negative zero and integer/float/bool distinctions. Dictionary order is immaterial.
+
+## Three prospective equality-only caller sites
+
+For the existing explicit Assets4MiB Audio literal profile only: AudioRawArchive.root_identity compares freshly read value with disk; _verify compares state with disk.state; _verify compares page-pinned value with pages[index]. Only the two json_digest calls whose results are used solely as equality would be replaced. Scope SHA, expected page SHA, literal/part SHA, range receipt and persisted references remain unchanged. Default1MiB path remains its original code. Every before/after physical/OFD/byte/stat/inventory and age call remains. No comparison result survives a call. No new budget/profile lane is proposed.
+
+## Callback and binding boundary
+
+The helper is callback-free for both freshly admitted exact builtin graphs: no descriptors, provider, JSON decoder, SDK, class binding, native clock or user predicate occurs between the two admissions and pair walk. Audio's page_store/path/stat work stays BEFORE this helper, so mutation at those boundaries is seen on BOTH current graphs. A right-side invalid graph may not bypass admission merely because the left differs.
+
+Before integration, the Assets-only call boundary must pin the original helper and canonical_size function identities, code objects/defaults/closure/global bindings and recheck them before and after invocation. Exact types precede any function attribute access. Unknown replacement refuses before calling a foreign function. The primitive comparison must not invoke foreign equality: admission rejects subclass scalars, containers and keys by type identity. This proposal does not pretend that a bare imported global is a complete binding barrier. The exact caller barrier hunk remains to be written/reviewed after this helper direction is accepted.
+
+## Finite counters before any integration
+
+Compare against current json_digest equality for valid exact trees including all ASCII controls, DEL, Unicode astral text, lone high/low surrogates, negative zero, int/float/bool, reordered keys and ordinary shared aliases. Both sides independently reject cycles, nonfinite numbers, container/scalar subclasses, deceptive metaclasses and foreign keys with zero foreign equality/descriptors. Genuine two-graph mutations must refuse; mismatching early scalar plus an invalid later graph still validates/refuses the latter. Helper/validator reference, code/default/closure replacement must refuse zero callbacks at the actual prospective caller.
+
+Retained current actual bank root/state/two page DTOs may supply a separate passive complete-predicate comparison on the same exact original bytes, with independent copies and all file hashes/eight-stat tuples stable. It supplies neither current-owner authority nor complete verify/whole performance. No quantitative win is promised: current measured Audio.verify128 calls551.199ms includes untouched physical and guard work and cannot be equated with JSON comparison cost.
+
+## Lifetime
+
+canonical_size already performs a fresh bounded traversal without whole serialization. The paired walk uses generator/recursive frames, no per-node retained metadata or second DTO copy. Before actual selection, bound peak recursive/generator stack versus the old canonical/type-walk transient under the SAME family; deep supported data must preserve acceptance or conservatively fall back to the old predicate without skipping admission. Do not infer freed credit from two digest expressions: their canonical buffers are sequential.
